{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.server.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.test-server.tsbuildinfo",
    /* The flag stays OFF for specs (#1301). A spec indexes fixtures it just built — `rows[0]` on an
       array it wrote two lines above — so `T | undefined` there is noise about a value the test
       itself guarantees. The value of the flag is in shipped code, which has it on. */
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  /* `test/helpers/**` is here because `appRequest.spec.ts` belonged to no project at all — a spec
     that nothing type-checked, and it had four findings waiting once something did (#1348). Claimed
     as a directory rather than by filename so the next server-side helper is covered the day it is
     written; a hand-maintained list is what orphaned this one.
     `xtermDouble.ts` and `cmEditorDouble.ts` are the browser half of the same directory — they
     name HTMLElement and document, or import a module that does, and neither exists under
     `types: ["node"]`. They are reached through the `test/src` specs that import them, so
     tsconfig.test.json checks them with the DOM lib they need. */
  /* `test/config/**` — specs over the root config files. They belong to the node-typed project
     rather than tsconfig.test.json because importing `vite.config.ts` into a DOM program pulls
     `@types/node`'s globals in beside the DOM ones, and `window.setTimeout` then resolves to
     Node's (a `Timeout`, not a `number`) in three unrelated components. */
  /* `test/docs/**` — specs that READ the repo's markdown off disk, so they need node types rather
     than the DOM. Listed because a spec in no project is type-checked by nothing and CI says so
     nowhere, which is the same hole `test/helpers` fell into above. */
  "include": [
    "test/docs/**/*.ts",
    "test/server/**/*.ts",
    "test/bin/**/*.ts",
    "test/scripts/**/*.ts",
    "test/config/**/*.ts",
    "test/support/**/*.ts",
    "test/helpers/**/*.ts",
    "server/**/*.spec.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["test/helpers/xtermDouble.ts", "test/helpers/cmEditorDouble.ts"]
}
